# Finance operating model (Slurp 2)

## Today (manual completion)
- Users complete Finance tasks **after** real-world confirmation (bank cleared, check sent, QuickBooks reconciled).
- Primary pattern: **Mark as paid** on AR/AP (date received/paid, optional reference) — not “record a speculative payment.”
- Completing a task **must** update operational records (AR/AP balances, invoice status) **and** post the matching journal / GL effects when accounts exist.
- Cash calendar / today’s tasks are operational surfaces into Mark as paid — not a separate accounting truth.
- Do **not** redesign or break the invoice create → issue → PDF pathway while evolving Finance.

## Later (bank-ready execution)
- Same UI actions should grow an **execution layer** (issue payment, transfer funds, ACH) without renaming or replacing Mark as paid for confirmation cases.
- Design payment / transfer services so a future bank connector can swap in for “manual marked complete,” not so the UI must be rebuilt.
- Prefer a single Payment (or similar) record with channel/status over parallel “manual vs bank” tables.

## Module placement
- **Home:** Finance home (embedded cash calendar, today’s mark-paid tasks, drafts). Full cash calendar via home; not a separate left-nav item.
- **Invoicing:** one workspace (`/finance/invoices/`) — Invoice register + Receivables tabs. Legacy `/finance/ar/` redirects. Create/issue/PDF unchanged.
- **Payables:** AP with Mark as paid.
- **Accounting:** GL, Journal, Fiscal periods, Bank recon (books layer).
- **Cost:** Costing workspace (`/finance/costing/`) — **What-if pricing** (Customer Pricing pipeline), Cost Master, R&D, RM lots. Customer **list** selling prices still live on Sales profiles; Finance what-if is the decision tool (margin/volume/cost).
- **Reports:** Financial Reports only in nav (P&L Actual / Pro-Forma / margin trends remain URL-reachable stubs if needed).
- Shipping KPIs → **Sales**. Customer payment timeliness → Sales customer **Payments**. Vendor payment timeliness → Quality vendor **Payments**.
